Win7 Asynchronous Page Swapping Support for Graphics Working Set:
Helped in a supporting role, DirectX and OS software teams design implement and debug a software pipeline that steals pages/resources from graphics processes that are idle and places acquires in their instruction pipeline to reclaim pages before next execution. My contribution was to inject stalling instructions in the instruction stream to do the stealing/reclamation part.

Windows 8 Mid Buffer Preemption to improve Graphics/Compute Interactivity:
The goal is to allow the OS to queue a long list of work buffers upfront to increase pipelining and prefetching gains yet let OS insert new work or change already inserted work on the fly with minimal overhead. My role was to design/implement and debug the instruction stream modification software with the necessary invalidates/flushes.  This project was eventually discarded because preemption latencies were unacceptable on current GPU hw. 
Working with closely with hw to improve graphics preemption latency for the Maxwell generation of GPUs.


